            "readingTime": "4 min",
            "explanation": "### How to Add JavaScript to an HTML Page\n\nThere are three ways to include JavaScript in HTML:\n\n#### 1. External Script File (Recommended Best Practice)\nKeep your HTML and JavaScript in separate files for clean separation of concerns:\n```html\n<!-- In index.html -->\n<script src=\"app.js\"></script>\n```\n\n#### 2. Internal Script Tag\nEmbed JavaScript directly inside a `<script>` element:\n```html\n<script>\n  console.log(\"Running inline JavaScript!\");\n</script>\n```\n\n#### 3. Where to Place the Script Tag?\nBest practice is placing `<script src=\"app.js\">` right before the closing `</body>` tag, or in the `<head>` with the `defer` attribute:\n```html\n<head>\n  <script src=\"app.js\" defer></script>\n</head>\n```\nThe `defer` attribute tells the browser to download the script in parallel while parsing HTML, and execute it only after the HTML document is fully parsed.",
