            "readingTime": "4 min",
            "explanation": "### JavaScript Syntax Rules\nJavaScript syntax is case-sensitive and follows standard C-family conventions.\n\n```javascript\n// Case sensitivity example\nlet learnerName = \"Amina\";\nlet LearnerName = \"Zaid\"; // Different variable!\n```\n\n### Semicolons (`;`)\nSemicolons terminate statements. While JavaScript has Automatic Semicolon Insertion (ASI), explicitly writing semicolons makes your intentions clear and prevents subtle edge-case bugs:\n```javascript\nconst greeting = \"Hello\";\nconsole.log(greeting);\n```\n\n### Comments in Code\nComments are ignored by the JavaScript engine and serve as documentation for developers:\n```javascript\n// Single-line comment: Explains what the next line does\nconst maxAttempts = 3;\n\n/* \n   Multi-line comment:\n   Useful for describing complex algorithms,\n   business rules, or API schemas.\n*/\nfunction calculateScore() {\n  return 100;\n}\n```",
