            "explanation": "### Rules for Variable Names\n1. Variable names must start with a letter, underscore (`_`), or dollar sign (`$`).\n2. Subsequent characters can include letters, numbers, underscores, and dollar signs.\n3. Variable names cannot start with a number (e.g. `1stPlayer` is invalid).\n4. Variable names cannot be reserved JavaScript keywords (`class`, `return`, `function`, `const`, etc.).\n\n### Conventions in JavaScript\n- **camelCase**: Standard for variables and function names (e.g. `learnerScore`, `isAuthenticated`, `totalPrice`).\n- **UPPER_SNAKE_CASE**: Reserved for global constant configuration values (e.g. `MAX_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS`, `API_BASE_URL`).\n- **Descriptive Names**: Avoid single letters like `x` or `d`. Prefer `userAge`, `downloadDurationInSeconds`.",
