            "explanation": "### Combining Boolean Expressions\n\n#### 1. Logical AND (`&&`)\nReturns `true` only if **ALL** conditions are `true`:\n```javascript\nconst hasPaid = true;\nconst isEnrolled = true;\n\nif (hasPaid && isEnrolled) {\n  console.log(\"Access course content\");\n}\n```\n\n#### 2. Logical OR (`||`)\nReturns `true` if **AT LEAST ONE** condition is `true`:\n```javascript\nconst isAdmin = false;\nconst isAuthor = true;\n\nif (isAdmin || isAuthor) {\n  console.log(\"Can edit lesson\");\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. Logical NOT (`!`)\nInverts a boolean value (`true` becomes `false`, `false` becomes `true`):\n```javascript\nconst isLocked = false;\nif (!isLocked) {\n  console.log(\"Door is open\");\n}\n```",
