            "explanation": "### Modern Iteration with `for...of`\nWhen you want to visit every element in an array without manually managing index numbers, use `for...of`:\n\n```javascript\nconst frameworks = [\"React\", \"Vue\", \"Svelte\"];\n\nfor (const framework of frameworks) {\n  console.log(`Framework: ${framework}`);\n}\n```\n\nIt is cleaner, less error-prone, and works on any iterable (Arrays, Strings, Sets, NodeLists).",
