          {
            "id": "js-8-4",
            "title": "Controlling Loops with `break` and `continue`",
            "subtitle": "Halting loops early and skipping specific iterations",
            "readingTime": "3 min",
            "explanation": "### `break` vs `continue`\n\n#### 1. `break` (Terminate Loop)\nImmediately exits the entire loop:\n```javascript\nfor (let i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {\n  if (i === 4) break; // Halts loop completely when i is 4\n  console.log(i); // Prints 1, 2, 3\n}\n```\n\n#### 2. `continue` (Skip Iteration)\nSkips the rest of the current iteration and jumps directly to the next one:\n```javascript\nfor (let i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {\n  if (i === 3) continue; // Skips number 3\n  console.log(i); // Prints 1, 2, 4, 5\n}\n```",
            "keyPoints": [
              "`break` terminates the surrounding loop entirely.",
              "`continue` skips the remainder of the current iteration and advances the counter.",
              "Use them to optimize search loops and skip invalid data items."
            ],
            "examples": [
              {
                "title": "Finding first target match and breaking",
                "code": "const numbers = [10, 25, 42, 60];\nfor (const num of numbers) {\n  if (num === 42) {\n    console.log(\"Found 42!\");\n    break;\n  }\n}",
                "description": "Exiting early once search goal is met."
              }
            ],
            "practice": "Write a loop that skips even numbers using `continue`.",
            "challenge": {
              "type": "quiz",
              "question": "What does the `continue` statement do inside a JavaScript loop?",
              "options": [
                "Restarts the entire loop from index 0.",
                "Skips the rest of the current iteration and advances to the next iteration.",
                "Exits the loop permanently.",
                "Throws an exception if a condition is met."
              ],
              "correctAnswer": 1,
              "explanation": "`continue` immediately skips remaining code in the current iteration and moves to the next loop cycle."
            }
          }
