            "readingTime": "5 min",
            "explanation": "### The `classList` API\nRather than writing inline styles with `element.style.color`, best practice is toggling CSS classes:\n\n```javascript\nconst modal = document.querySelector(\".modal\");\n\n// 1. Add class\nmodal.classList.add(\"is-visible\");\n\n// 2. Remove class\nmodal.classList.remove(\"hidden\");\n\n// 3. Toggle class (adds if missing, removes if present)\nmodal.classList.toggle(\"dark-mode\");\n\n// 4. Check if class exists\nif (modal.classList.contains(\"is-visible\")) {\n  console.log(\"Modal is open\");\n}\n```",
