            "title": "Intercepting Form Submits (`e.preventDefault()`)",
            "subtitle": "Preventing full page reloads on form submissions",
            "readingTime": "4 min",
            "explanation": "### Why Forms Reload the Page\nBy default, submitting an HTML `<form>` initiates an HTTP request and reloads the browser page. In modern Single Page Applications (SPAs) and JavaScript apps, we intercept this:\n\n```javascript\nconst form = document.querySelector(\"#cert-form\");\n\nform.addEventListener(\"submit\", (e) => {\n  e.preventDefault(); // HALTS the browser page reload!\n  console.log(\"Form submitted smoothly via JavaScript.\");\n});\n```\n\nAfter calling `e.preventDefault()`, JavaScript maintains full control to validate, process, and send data asynchronously.",
            "keyPoints": [
              "Always attach the submit listener to the `<form>` element itself, not just a button.",
              "`e.preventDefault()` stops the default browser form submission refresh.",
              "Submitting via Enter key or submit button both trigger the form's `submit` event."
            ],
            "examples": [
              {
                "title": "Basic form submission intercept",
                "code": "const loginForm = document.querySelector(\"#login-form\");\nloginForm.addEventListener(\"submit\", (e) => {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  const email = loginForm.elements[\"email\"].value;\n  authenticateUser(email);\n});",
                "description": "Intercepting form submission to handle authentication via API."
              }
            ],
            "practice": "Write a form submit handler that uses `e.preventDefault()` to keep the page intact.",
            "challenge": {
              "type": "quiz",
              "question": "What is the purpose of `e.preventDefault()` inside a form 'submit' event handler?",
              "options": [
                "It clears all input fields automatically.",
                "It prevents the browser from refreshing and reloading the page.",
                "It encrypts form data using SSL.",
                "It disables the submit button permanently."
              ],
              "correctAnswer": 1,
              "explanation": "`e.preventDefault()` stops the browser's default action, which for forms is a full page reload."
            }
