        "readingTime": "22 min",
        "summary": "Ingest and export diverse commercial datasets using pandas. Master pd.read_csv parameters (encoding, separators, date parsing), read multi-tab Excel files, parse nested JSON APIs, and query SQL databases directly into DataFrames.",
        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this module, you will be able to:\n1. Ingest flat files using **`pd.read_csv()`** with custom delimiters, character encodings (`utf-8`, `latin1`), and date parsers.\n2. Read and write multi-sheet Microsoft Excel workbooks using **`pd.read_excel()`** and **`pd.ExcelWriter()`**.\n3. Ingest hierarchical JSON from REST APIs and flatten nested payloads using **`pd.json_normalize()`**.\n4. Connect to relational SQL databases (PostgreSQL, SQLite, MySQL) and load query results into DataFrames with **`pd.read_sql()`**.\n5. Export cleaned DataFrames to high-performance Parquet, CSV, and Excel formats.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Ingesting CSV Files with Real-World Parameters\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndf_sales = pd.read_csv(\n    \"nairobi_retail_sales_2026.csv\",\n    sep=\",\",                          # Delimiter\n    parse_dates=[\"transaction_date\"], # Automatically coerce to datetime64\n    dtype={\"customer_phone\": str},    # Prevent stripping leading zeros (e.g. 0712...)\n    na_values=[\"N/A\", \"missing\", \"-\"],# Coerce dirty placeholders to np.nan\n    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n)\n\n# Inspect DataFrame shape and memory consumption\nprint(df_sales.info())\nprint(df_sales.head(5))\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Querying SQL Databases Directly into pandas\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\n\n# 1. Create database connection engine\nengine = create_engine(\"postgresql://analyst:secret@localhost:5432/commercial_db\")\n\n# 2. Execute SQL query directly into a pandas DataFrame\nsql_query = \"\"\"\n    SELECT \n        customer_id, \n        branch_name, \n        SUM(amount_ksh) AS total_spend_ksh\n    FROM transactions\n    WHERE status = 'Completed'\n    GROUP BY customer_id, branch_name\n\"\"\"\n\ndf_customer_summary = pd.read_sql(sql_query, con=engine)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary & Best Practices\n- Always specify `dtype={'phone': str, 'id': str}` for ID and phone columns to prevent pandas from coercing them into numeric integers and dropping leading zeros.\n- Use **Parquet format** (`df.to_parquet('data.parquet')`) for large datasets to achieve 5x faster read speeds and 80% smaller file sizes compared to CSV.",
