        "summary": "Master the twin pillars of pandas: Series and DataFrames. Learn label-based indexing (.loc) vs integer position indexing (.iloc), boolean masking, dynamic column creation, and multi-column sorting.",
        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this module, you will be able to:\n1. Explain the anatomy of a **pandas DataFrame** (Index, Columns, Values, Data Types).\n2. Differentiate between a 1D **Series** and a 2D **DataFrame**.\n3. Master label-based selection (**`.loc`**) vs zero-indexed integer positional selection (**`.iloc`**).\n4. Filter rows with complex **Boolean Masking** using bitwise operators (`&` for AND, `|` for OR, `~` for NOT).\n5. Add, rename, reorder, and drop columns safely without mutating source data unexpectedly.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Label Selection (.loc) vs Positional Selection (.iloc)\n\n```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                             .loc vs .iloc SELECTION                           |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Method | Selection Mechanism           | Example Syntax                       |\n+--------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------+\n| .loc   | By Label / Column Name / Mask | df.loc[df['city'] == 'Nairobi', 'rev']|\n| .iloc  | By Integer Position (0, 1, 2) | df.iloc[0:5, 1:4]                    |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndata = {\n    \"branch\": [\"Nairobi CBD\", \"Mombasa Port\", \"Kisumu City\", \"Eldoret Town\"],\n    \"revenue_ksh\": [12500000, 8900000, 6400000, 5100000],\n    \"manager\": [\"Kamau\", \"Hassan\", \"Otieno\", \"Cheruiyot\"]\n}\ndf = pd.DataFrame(data)\n\n# Select first 2 rows and first 2 columns by position\nprint(df.iloc[0:2, 0:2])\n\n# Select branches with revenue > KSh 7,000,000 by label\nhigh_rev = df.loc[df[\"revenue_ksh\"] > 7000000, [\"branch\", \"revenue_ksh\"]]\nprint(high_rev)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Multi-Condition Boolean Filtering\n\n> **Crucial Syntax Rule**: When combining conditions in pandas, you **must wrap each condition in parentheses** and use bitwise operators (`&`, `|`):\n\n```python\n# Correct:\nnairobi_wholesale = df_orders.loc[\n    (df_orders[\"region\"] == \"Nairobi\") & (df_orders[\"customer_segment\"] == \"Wholesale\")\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary & Best Practices\n- Always use `.loc` when filtering rows and selecting specific column names simultaneously.\n- Always use parentheses around boolean conditions: `(df['A'] > 10) & (df['B'] == 'Yes')`.",
