        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this module, you will be able to:\n1. Understand the **Object-Oriented Architecture** of Matplotlib (`fig, ax = plt.subplots()`).\n2. Build statistical distributions and histograms with **Seaborn (`sns.histplot`, `sns.kdeplot`)**.\n3. Identify outliers and compare categorical spreads using **Box Plots (`sns.boxplot`)** and **Violin Plots**.\n4. Visualize multivariate correlations using **Scatter Plots (`sns.scatterplot`)** with hue and size encodings.\n5. Compute correlation matrices and plot annotated **Heatmaps (`sns.heatmap`)**.\n6. Format clean labels, legends, titles, and export high-resolution vector figures (`dpi=300`).\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Matplotlib Object-Oriented Architecture\n\n```python\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\n\n# Set professional theme\nsns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", palette=\"muted\")\n\n# 1. Create Canvas (Figure) and Coordinate Systems (Axes)\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6), dpi=150)\n\n# 2. Plot on the Axis using Seaborn\nsns.barplot(\n    data=branch_summary,\n    x=\"branch_name\",\n    y=\"total_revenue_ksh\",\n    palette=\"Blues_d\",\n    ax=ax\n)\n\n# 3. Add Executive Formatting\nax.set_title(\"Nairobi & Regional Outlets: Q1 2026 Revenue (KSh)\", fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\", pad=15)\nax.set_xlabel(\"Regional Commercial Hub\", fontsize=11)\nax.set_ylabel(\"Gross Revenue (KSh)\", fontsize=11)\nax.yaxis.set_major_formatter('{x:,.0f}')\nplt.xticks(rotation=15)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Correlation Matrix Heatmap\n\n```python\n# Compute Pearson correlation matrix across numerical metrics\nnumerical_cols = [\"amount_ksh\", \"discount_ksh\", \"delivery_time_hours\", \"customer_satisfaction_score\"]\ncorr_matrix = df[numerical_cols].corr()\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\nsns.heatmap(\n    corr_matrix, \n    annot=True,          # Show numerical correlation coefficients (-1.0 to +1.0)\n    cmap=\"coolwarm\",     # Blue = Negative correlation, Red = Positive correlation\n    fmt=\".2f\",\n    linewidths=1.0,\n    cbar=True\n)\nplt.title(\"Commercial Performance Feature Correlation Matrix\", fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary & Best Practices\n- Always use `fig, ax = plt.subplots()` to ensure full programmatic control over chart elements.\n- Annotate exact values on bar charts so stakeholders do not have to estimate heights from the Y-axis.",
