        "number": 8,
        "title": "Technical Interview Preparation, Live Case Studies, and Salary Negotiation",
        "subtitle": "Live SQL whiteboard coding, Python take-homes, behavioral STAR responses, and salary negotiation strategies",
        "readingTime": "24 min",
        "summary": "Ace the end-to-end data analyst hiring pipeline. Master live SQL live-coding tests, Python wrangling take-home assignments, behavioral STAR interview frameworks, and negotiate above-market compensation packages with confidence.",
        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this module, you will be able to:\n1. Prepare for and pass the 4 standard interview stages: **Recruiter Screen** -> **Technical Assessment (SQL/Python)** -> **Business Case Study Presentation** -> **Executive Cultural Fit**.\n2. Solve live SQL coding challenges under pressure (joins, window functions, aggregations) while explaining your thought process out loud.\n3. Structure behavioral interview answers using the **STAR Method** (Situation, Task, Action, Result).\n4. Complete and present 48-hour take-home business case studies that blow interviewers away.\n5. Confidently negotiate base salary, signing bonuses, flexible remote work terms, and professional development stipends.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The 4 Golden Rules of Live SQL Technical Interviews\n\n1. **Clarify Before Coding**: Ask about edge cases: \"Are there duplicate customer IDs? Can transaction amounts be NULL or negative?\"\n2. **Talk Through Your Logic Out Loud**: Interviewers evaluate your analytical reasoning even if you make a minor syntax typo.\n3. **Start with the Core Aggregation**: Write the `FROM` and `JOIN` clauses first, then `WHERE`, then `GROUP BY`.\n4. **Test and Sanity Check**: Walk through sample rows manually before saying \"I am finished\".\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Behavioral STAR Framework\n\nWhen asked: *\"Tell me about a time you found an unexpected anomaly in the data\"*:\n- **Situation**: \"While auditing Q4 payment reconciliation logs across 12 branch outlets...\"\n- **Task**: \"I needed to investigate why KSh 1.8M in reported sales was missing from bank settlements.\"\n- **Action**: \"I authored a PostgreSQL CTE anti-join comparing POS cash till records against M-Pesa merchant statement APIs and isolated a webhook timeout bug on weekend shifts.\"\n- **Result**: \"We patched the webhook retry queue, recovered 100% of the untracked revenue, and automated daily automated mismatch alerts.\"\n\n---\n\n### 3. Confident Salary Negotiation Principles\n\n- **Never Give the First Number Early**: When asked for salary expectations during screening, say: *\"I am focused on finding the right mutual fit. I'd love to learn more about the role's scope before discussing specific compensation packages.\"*\n- **Know Market Rates**: In Kenya and remote international markets, benchmark salaries using industry reports and FAHMRISE career guidelines.\n- **Negotiate the Total Package**: Base salary, annual performance bonuses, remote work allowances, healthcare coverage, and training budgets.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Final Course Wrap-Up & Verified Certificate Eligibility\n\nCongratulations on completing the **Data Analytics Portfolio & Career Preparation** curriculum!\n- You have mastered commercial problem framing, KPI metrics tree design, executive storytelling, GitHub portfolio architecture, multi-tool showcase builds, ATS CV crafting, and technical interview mastery.\n- Mark this final lesson complete in your dashboard to unlock your official **Verified FAHMRISE Certificate of Completion in Data Analytics Portfolio & Career Preparation**.",
