        "number": 10,
        "title": "Final Practical Capstone Project: End-to-End Business Analysis",
        "subtitle": "Clean an enterprise multi-channel dataset, perform complex analytical modeling, build an interactive PivotTable dashboard, and deliver board recommendations",
        "readingTime": "30 min",
        "summary": "Execute an end-to-end analytical project from raw data ingestion to executive presentation: audit data quality, build automated cleaning pipelines, model multi-condition KPIs, assemble an interactive dashboard with Slicers, and deliver strategic recommendations.",
        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this capstone module, you will be able to:\n1. Conduct an end-to-end data analysis project following professional enterprise workflows.\n2. Ingest, audit, and clean a messy 1,000+ record commercial business dataset.\n3. Apply advanced mathematical, logical, lookup, and time-series formulas to model business performance.\n4. Construct an interactive multi-PivotTable dashboard with synchronized Slicers and Sparklines.\n5. Author a comprehensive Executive Summary Report with data-backed strategic recommendations.\n6. Claim your official Verified FAHMRISE Certificate of Completion in Data Analysis & Spreadsheet Mastery.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Capstone Business Scenario: \"Zawadi Retail Enterprises Kenya\"\n\n**Zawadi Retail Enterprises Kenya** is a growing omnichannel retail business operating 5 regional retail and wholesale distribution hubs across Kenya:\n- **Nairobi (Headquarters & Central Hub)**\n- **Mombasa (Coast Hub)**\n- **Kisumu (Lake Basin Hub)**\n- **Nakuru (Rift Valley Hub)**\n- **Eldoret (North Rift Hub)**\n\nThe company sells four core product categories:\n1. **Electronics & Tech Accessories**\n2. **Home & Kitchen Appliances**\n3. **Packaged Groceries & Fast-Moving Consumer Goods (FMCG)**\n4. **Fashion & Apparel**\n\nPayments are collected across four channels: **M-Pesa Paybill / Till**, **Visa/Mastercard Card**, **Direct Bank Transfer**, and **Cash**.\n\nAs the Lead Commercial Data Analyst, you have received the raw annual transaction export `Zawadi_Raw_Sales_2026.csv`. The Board of Directors has tasked you with conducting an end-to-end audit, uncovering profitability drivers, building an interactive management dashboard, and presenting actionable recommendations for 2027 expansion.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Phase 1: Raw Data Ingestion & Quality Audit\n\nInspect the raw transaction schema:\n\n| Raw Invoice ID | Raw Date String | Branch | Product Category | Customer Type | Quantity Sold | Unit Price (KSh) | Discount Applied | Payment Method | Delivery Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **INV-9011** | 2026-01-05 | Nairobi | Electronics | 'Retail' | 4 | KSh 4,500.00 | 0.05 | mpesa | Delivered |\n| **INV-9012** | 2026-01-05 |  Mombasa  | Home & Kitchen | Wholesale | 12 | 8200 | 0.10 | Card | Delivered |\n| **INV-9013** | 06.01.2026 | Nbi | FMCG | 'Retail' | 45 | KSh 350.00 | 0.00 | M-Pesa | Delivered |\n| **INV-9014** | 2026-01-08 | Kisumu | Fashion | Retail | 8 | 2400 | 0.00 | cash | Returned |\n| **INV-9015** | 2026-01-09 | Eldoret | Electronics | Wholesale | 15 | KSh 12,000.00 | 0.08 | Bank Transfer | Delivered |\n\n#### Audit Checklist (6 Critical Data Quality Issues Detected):\n1. **Branch Names**: Mixed aliases and whitespace (`\"Nbi\"`, `\" Nairobi \"`, `\"Mombasa \"`).\n2. **Date Inconsistency**: Mixed ISO format (`2026-01-05`) and European dot format text strings (`06.01.2026`).\n3. **Unit Price Format**: Inconsistent currency text (`\"KSh 4,500.00\"`) mixed with raw numbers (`8200`).\n4. **Customer Types**: Leading/trailing single quotes (`'Retail'`).\n5. **Payment Method Casing**: Mixed casing (`\"mpesa\"`, `\"M-Pesa\"`, `\"cash\"`, `\"Card\"`).\n6. **Duplicate Invoices**: Several duplicated billing transactions requiring detection and elimination.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Phase 2: Data Cleaning & Sanitization Pipeline\n\nBuild clean columns on a new worksheet named `Clean_Data`:\n\n1. **Clean Date**:\n   ```excel\n   =IF(ISNUMBER(B2), B2, DATEVALUE(SUBSTITUTE(B2, \".\", \"/\")))\n   ```\n2. **Clean Branch**:\n   ```excel\n   =XLOOKUP(TRIM(C2), Branch_Mapping[Raw], Branch_Mapping[Clean], PROPER(TRIM(C2)))\n   ```\n3. **Clean Customer Type**:\n   ```excel\n   =SUBSTITUTE(TRIM(E2), \"'\", \"\")\n   ```\n4. **Clean Unit Price**:\n   ```excel\n   =IF(ISNUMBER(G2), G2, VALUE(SUBSTITUTE(SUBSTITUTE(G2, \"KSh\", \"\"), \",\", \"\")))\n   ```\n5. **Clean Payment Method**:\n   ```excel\n   =PROPER(TRIM(I2))\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Phase 3: Analytical Formulas & KPI Computations\n\nAdd calculated financial metrics across the clean table:\n1. **Gross Revenue**: `=[@QuantitySold] * [@UnitPrice]`\n2. **Discount Amount**: `=[@GrossRevenue] * [@DiscountApplied]`\n3. **Net Revenue**: `=[@GrossRevenue] - [@DiscountAmount]`\n4. **Cost of Goods Sold (COGS)** (Looked up from `Product_Master`):\n   ```excel\n   =XLOOKUP([@ProductCategory], Product_Master[Category], Product_Master[UnitCost]) * [@QuantitySold]\n   ```\n5. **Gross Profit**: `=[@NetRevenue] - [@COGS]`\n6. **Gross Margin %**: `=[@GrossProfit] / [@NetRevenue]`\n\n---\n\n### 5. Phase 4: Multi-Dimensional PivotTable Architecture\n\nBuild 4 dedicated PivotTables on worksheet `Analytics_Pivot`:\n- **Pivot 1 (Branch Matrix)**: Rows = `Branch`, Columns = `Quarter`, Values = `Sum of Net Revenue`, `Average Profit Margin %`.\n- **Pivot 2 (Category Profitability)**: Rows = `Product Category`, Values = `Net Revenue`, `Gross Profit`, `% of Total Revenue`.\n- **Pivot 3 (Payment Channel Distribution)**: Rows = `Payment Method`, Values = `Transaction Count`, `Total Revenue`, `% of Column Total`.\n- **Pivot 4 (Customer Segmentation)**: Rows = `Customer Type`, Values = `Average Order Value`, `Total Orders`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Phase 5: Assembling the Executive Interactive Dashboard\n\nDesign the `Executive_Dashboard` presentation view:\n1. **4 Top KPI Cards**:\n   - **Total Net Revenue**: `KSh 148,520,000.00`\n   - **Total Gross Profit**: `KSh 48,120,000.00` (Average Margin: `32.4%`)\n   - **Total Orders Delivered**: `18,450 Orders` (Delivery Rate: `97.2%`)\n   - **Average Order Value (AOV)**: `KSh 8,049.00`\n2. **Visuals**:\n   - Monthly Net Revenue vs Budget Target (Combo Chart).\n   - Regional Profit Contribution by Branch (Horizontal Clustered Bar Chart).\n   - Category Share of Revenue (Donut Chart).\n3. **Interactivity**:\n   - Insert Slicers for **Branch**, **Quarter**, and **Customer Type**.\n   - Enable **Report Connections** across all 4 PivotTables.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Phase 6: Strategic Executive Memo to the Board\n\n#### Headline Findings:\n1. **Nairobi & Mombasa Hubs**: Contributed 64.2% of total revenue and 71% of net profit, driven by high wholesale tech demand.\n2. **Payment Channel Dominance**: M-Pesa accounted for 68.4% of retail transaction count and 52.1% of revenue volume with zero settlement delay.\n3. **Eldoret & Kisumu Expansion Opportunity**: Fashion and Home Appliances exhibited a high 41.2% gross margin but suffered from periodic inventory stockouts.\n\n#### Strategic Recommendations:\n1. **Supply Chain Optimization**: Establish a dedicated central restocking depot in Nakuru to reduce transit turnaround to Eldoret and Kisumu from 6 days to 2 days.\n2. **Wholesale Sourcing Negotiations**: Leverage volume growth in Electronics to negotiate an additional 4% supplier rebate.\n3. **Direct M-Pesa Merchant Integration**: Automate point-of-sale M-Pesa STK Push across all checkout counters to reduce counter queue times by 35%.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Final Capstone Submission & Certificate Eligibility\n\nCongratulations on completing the **Data Analysis & Spreadsheet Mastery** curriculum!\n- You have mastered foundational grid architecture, tidy data structures, formula engines, advanced lookups, sanitization workflows, PivotTables, visualization psychology, KPI dashboards, and board-level executive reporting.\n- Mark this final capstone lesson complete in your dashboard to unlock your official **Verified FAHMRISE Certificate of Completion in Data Analysis & Spreadsheet Mastery**.",
