        "number": 10,
        "title": "Practical Python Capstone Project: End-to-End Commercial Data Pipeline",
        "subtitle": "Nairobi Logistics & E-Commerce: Ingestion, automated cleaning, customer cohort retention, and executive report export",
        "readingTime": "30 min",
        "summary": "Apply all Python, pandas, NumPy, and Seaborn skills into an end-to-end Capstone Project. Cleanse raw messy transaction files, compute customer cohort retention metrics, generate high-resolution visual charts, and export executive summary datasets.",
        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this module, you will be able to:\n1. Construct a fully automated end-to-end Python data pipeline from raw file ingestion to executive report delivery.\n2. Implement custom sanitization pipelines resolving dirty strings, inconsistent date timestamps, and missing values.\n3. Compute customer cohort retention curves and month-over-month revenue growth velocities in pandas.\n4. Generate a multi-panel exploratory visualization dashboard saved as publication-ready PNG artifacts.\n5. Export cleaned analytical datasets to Excel and Parquet formats.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Capstone Scenario: \"Nairobi Logistics & E-Commerce Kenya\"\n\n**Nairobi Express Direct** is an omnichannel e-commerce retail platform serving customers across Kenya through door-to-door courier delivery and M-Pesa automated merchant checkout.\n\n#### Project Deliverables:\n1. **Automated ETL Script**: Read messy CSVs, coerce data types, strip currency symbols, impute missing values.\n2. **Customer Cohort Retention Engine**: Track monthly repeat purchase retention curves across customer registration cohorts.\n3. **Multi-Panel Executive Plot**: 4-panel Seaborn figure showing Revenue Trends, Payment Channel Share, Regional Margins, and Delivery Turnaround vs Customer Satisfaction.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Capstone Pipeline Script\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\n\n# =============================================================================\n# STAGE 1: INGESTION & DATA CLEANING PIPELINE\n# =============================================================================\ndef load_and_sanitize_data(filepath: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    # 1. Load raw file\n    df = pd.read_csv(filepath)\n    \n    # 2. Standardize column names\n    df.columns = df.columns.str.strip().str.lower().str.replace(\" \", \"_\")\n    \n    # 3. Clean currency strings\n    for col in [\"unit_price\", \"unit_cost\", \"discount\", \"total_amount\"]:\n        if col in df.columns:\n            df[col] = df[col].astype(str).str.replace(\"KSh\", \"\").str.replace(\",\", \"\").str.strip()\n            df[col] = pd.to_numeric(df[col], errors=\"coerce\").fillna(0.0)\n            \n    # 4. Coerce timestamps\n    df[\"order_date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"order_date\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n    df = df.dropna(subset=[\"order_date\", \"customer_id\"])\n    \n    # 5. Feature Engineering\n    df[\"sales_month\"] = df[\"order_date\"].dt.to_period(\"M\")\n    df[\"gross_profit_ksh\"] = (df[\"total_amount\"] - (df[\"quantity\"] * df[\"unit_cost\"]))\n    df[\"gross_margin_pct\"] = np.where(\n        df[\"total_amount\"] > 0, \n        (df[\"gross_profit_ksh\"] / df[\"total_amount\"]) * 100, \n        0.0\n    )\n    \n    return df\n\n# =============================================================================\n# STAGE 2: COHORT RETENTION ENGINE\n# =============================================================================\ndef compute_cohort_retention(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    # Assign acquisition cohort month to each customer\n    df[\"cohort_month\"] = df.groupby(\"customer_id\")[\"sales_month\"].transform(\"min\")\n    \n    # Calculate cohort index (month 0, month 1, month 2...)\n    df[\"cohort_index\"] = (df[\"sales_month\"] - df[\"cohort_month\"]).apply(lambda x: x.n)\n    \n    # Group by cohort and index\n    cohort_data = df.groupby([\"cohort_month\", \"cohort_index\"])[\"customer_id\"].nunique().reset_index()\n    cohort_pivot = cohort_data.pivot(index=\"cohort_month\", columns=\"cohort_index\", values=\"customer_id\")\n    \n    # Calculate retention percentage relative to cohort size at Month 0\n    cohort_size = cohort_pivot.iloc[:, 0]\n    retention_matrix = cohort_pivot.divide(cohort_size, axis=0) * 100\n    return retention_matrix\n\n# =============================================================================\n# STAGE 3: EXECUTIVE VISUALIZATION SUITE\n# =============================================================================\ndef generate_executive_dashboard(df: pd.DataFrame):\n    sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10), dpi=150)\n    \n    # 1. Monthly Revenue & Profit Trend\n    monthly = df.groupby(\"sales_month\").agg(\n        revenue=(\"total_amount\", \"sum\"),\n        profit=(\"gross_profit_ksh\", \"sum\")\n    ).reset_index()\n    monthly[\"sales_month_str\"] = monthly[\"sales_month\"].astype(str)\n    \n    axes[0, 0].plot(monthly[\"sales_month_str\"], monthly[\"revenue\"] / 1e6, marker=\"o\", color=\"#0284c7\", label=\"Revenue (M KSh)\")\n    axes[0, 0].plot(monthly[\"sales_month_str\"], monthly[\"profit\"] / 1e6, marker=\"s\", color=\"#10b981\", label=\"Profit (M KSh)\")\n    axes[0, 0].set_title(\"Monthly Revenue & Gross Profit Trend\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n    axes[0, 0].set_ylabel(\"Millions (KSh)\")\n    axes[0, 0].legend()\n    \n    # 2. Payment Channel Share\n    payment_counts = df[\"payment_channel\"].value_counts()\n    axes[0, 1].pie(payment_counts, labels=payment_counts.index, autopct=\"%1.1f%%\", colors=[\"#10b981\", \"#38bdf8\", \"#f59e0b\"], startangle=140)\n    axes[0, 1].set_title(\"Transaction Volume by Payment Channel\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n    \n    # 3. Regional Profit Margins\n    sns.barplot(data=df, x=\"region\", y=\"gross_margin_pct\", ax=axes[1, 0], palette=\"crest\", ci=None)\n    axes[1, 0].set_title(\"Average Gross Margin % by Region\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n    axes[1, 0].set_ylabel(\"Gross Margin (%)\")\n    \n    # 4. Delivery Turnaround vs Satisfaction Correlation\n    sns.regplot(data=df, x=\"delivery_hours\", y=\"satisfaction_score\", ax=axes[1, 1], scatter_kws={\"alpha\":0.3, \"color\":\"#6366f1\"}, line_kws={\"color\":\"#ef4444\"})\n    axes[1, 1].set_title(\"Impact of Delivery Speed on Customer Satisfaction\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n    axes[1, 1].set_xlabel(\"Delivery Turnaround (Hours)\")\n    axes[1, 1].set_ylabel(\"Rating (1 to 5 Stars)\")\n    \n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(\"executive_analytics_dashboard.png\")\n    print(\"Executive dashboard saved successfully to executive_analytics_dashboard.png\")\n\nprint(\"Python Analytics Capstone Engine Ready.\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Final Capstone Submission & Certificate Eligibility\n\nCongratulations on completing the **Python for Data Analysis** curriculum!\n- You have mastered Python data structures, modular functions, NumPy vectorization, pandas DataFrame manipulation, data sanitization, relational merging, exploratory statistical visualization, and automated data pipelines.\n- Mark this final capstone lesson complete in your dashboard to unlock your official **Verified FAHMRISE Certificate of Completion in Python for Data Analysis**.",
