        "content": "\n# Module 3C: Social Justice, Gratitude & Divine Power\n\nIslam unites pure monotheism (*Haqq Allah*) with uncompromising compassion and justice toward fellow human beings (*Huquq al-'Ibad*). These four Surahs illustrate this vital integration.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Surah Al-Ma'un (Chapter 107): The Reality of True Faith\n\n```\n1. أَرَءَيْتَ ٱلَّذِى يُكَذِّبُ بِٱلدِّينِ\n2. فَذَٰلِكَ ٱلَّذِى يَدُعُّ ٱلْيَتِيمَ\n3. وَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلْمِسْكِينِ\n4. فَوَيْلٌ لِّلْمُصَلِّينَ\n5. ٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ عَن صَلَاتِهِمْ سَاهُونَ\n6. ٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ يُرَآءُونَ\n7. وَيَمْنَعُونَ ٱلْمَاعُونَ\n```\n\n> *\"Have you seen the one who denies the Recompense? That is the one who repulses the orphan, and does not encourage the feeding of the poor. So woe to those who pray [but] who are heedless of their prayer — those who make a show [of their deeds] and withhold simple assistance.\"*\n\n### Key Tafsir Insights:\n- **Faith Manifested in Action**: Denying the Day of Judgment is not merely a theoretical stance; it is reflected in callousness toward orphans (*Yatim*) and the destitute (*Miskin*).\n- **Heedlessness in Salah (*Sahoon*)**: Scholars note this includes those who deliberately delay prayer until its time expires, pray mechanically without thought, or abandon it entirely.\n- **Hypocrisy (*Riya'*) vs. Cruelty**: They perform deeds outward for public praise (*Yura'un*), yet refuse to lend the smallest neighborly necessities (*Al-Ma'un*).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Surah Quraysh (Chapter 106): Sustenance, Security & Gratitude\n\n```\n1. لِإِيلَـٰفِ قُرَيْشٍ\n2. إِيلَـٰفِهِمْ رِحْلَةَ ٱلشِّتَآءِ وَٱلصَّيْفِ\n3. فَلْيَعْبُدُوا۟ رَبَّ هَـٰذَا ٱلْبَيْتِ\n4. ٱلَّذِىٓ أَطْعَمَهُم مِّن جُوعٍ وَءَامَنَهُم مِّنْ خَوْفٍۭ\n```\n\n> *\"For the accustomed security of Quraysh — their accustomed security in the caravan of winter and summer — let them worship the Lord of this House, who has fed them, [saving them] from hunger and made them safe, [saving them] from fear.\"*\n\n### Key Tafsir Insights:\n- **The Twin Pillars of Civil Society**: **Freedom from hunger** (economic stability) and **freedom from fear** (peace and security).\n- **The Obligation of Worship**: In return for these immense divine blessings, humanity is obligated to worship the Lord of the Ka'bah (*Rabb hadha al-Bayt*) exclusively without associating partners.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Surah Al-Fil (Chapter 105): The Year of the Elephant\n\n```\n1. أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِأَصْحَـٰبِ ٱلْفِيلِ\n2. أَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ كَيْدَهُمْ فِى تَضْلِيلٍ\n3. وَأَرْسَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ طَيْرًا أَبَابِيلَ\n4. تَرْمِيهِم بِحِجَارَةٍ مِّن سِجِّيلٍ\n5. فَجَعَلَهُمْ كَعَصْفٍ مَّأْكُولٍۭ\n```\n\n> *\"Have you not considered, [O Muhammad], how your Lord dealt with the companions of the elephant? Did He not make their plan into misguidance? And He sent against them birds in flocks, striking them with stones of hard clay, and He made them like eaten straw.\"*\n\n### Key Tafsir Insights:\n- **Historical Event**: In 570 CE (the year Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was born), the Abyssinian ruler Abrahah marched with a formidable army and war elephants to demolish the Ka'bah.\n- **Divine Defense**: Allah destroyed the tyrant's army with flocks of birds (*Tayran Ababil*) carrying baked stones (*Sijjil*), reducing them to crushed straw (*'Asfin Ma'kul*).\n- **Lesson**: Human military might is powerless before the decree of Allah Almighty.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Surah Al-Humazah (Chapter 104): The Peril of Slander & Greed\n\n```\n1. وَيْلٌ لِّكُلِّ هُمَزَةٍ لُّمَزَةٍ\n2. ٱلَّذِى جَمَعَ مَالًا وَعَدَّدَهُۥ\n3. يَحْسَبُ أَنَّ مَالَهُۥٓ أَخْلَدَهُۥ\n4. كَلَّا ۖ لَيُنۢبَذَنَّ فِى ٱلْحُطَمَةِ\n5. وَمَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا ٱلْحُطَمَةُ\n6. نَارُ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُوقَدَةُ\n7. ٱلَّتِى تَطَّلِعُ عَلَى ٱلْأَفْـِٔدَةِ\n8. إِنَّهَا عَلَيْهِم مُّؤْصَدَةٌ\n9. فِى عَمَدٍ مُّمَدَّدَةٍۭ\n```\n\n> *\"Woe to every scorner and mocker who collects wealth and [continuously] counts it. He thinks that his wealth will make him immortal. No! He will surely be thrown into the Crusher (Al-Hutamah)...\"*\n\n### Key Tafsir Insights:\n- **Humazah vs. Lumazah**: Those who mock, slander, and look down upon others with arrogance.\n- **Illusion of Immortality**: Hoarding wealth deludes the owner into thinking material possessions confer eternal security.\n- **Al-Hutamah**: The blazing fire of Allah that reaches the depths of the heart (*Al-Af'idah*), matching the inner arrogance of the slanderer.\n",
