        "content": "\n# Module 4: Step-by-Step Practical Guide to Performing Salah\n\nFollow this comprehensive, illustrated guide to perform your prayer from beginning to end with exactitude.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Preparing to Stand Before Allah\n\n* Ensure your Wudu is valid, your Awrah is covered, your clothes are clean, and you are facing the **Qiblah** (towards the Ka'bah).\n* Stand upright (*Qiyam*), feet shoulder-width apart, and direct your gaze downward toward the spot where your forehead will touch in prostration.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Step-by-Step Breakdown of a Rak'ah (Unit of Prayer)\n\n### Step 1: Opening Takbir (*Takbirat al-Ihram*)\n* Raise both hands to shoulder or earlobe level, palms facing forward towards the Qiblah.\n* Say: **«اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ»** (*\"Allahu Akbar\"* — Allah is the Greatest).\n* Place your right hand over your left hand upon your chest or upper torso.\n\n### Step 2: Recitation\n* Quietly recite the opening supplication (*Du'a al-Istiftah*), followed by:\n  * *«أَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيمِ»* (I seek refuge in Allah from Satan the outcast).\n  * *«بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ»*.\n* Recite **Surah Al-Fatihah** verse by verse. At the end say: *«آمِين»* (*\"Ameen\"* — O Allah, accept).\n* In the first two Rak'ahs, recite any additional short Surah or passage (e.g. Surah Al-Ikhlas or Al-Kawthar).\n\n### Step 3: Bowing (*Ar-Ruku'*)\n* Say *«اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ»* and bow your torso downward.\n* Keep your back flat and level, placing your hands firmly on your knees with fingers spread, looking down at your feet.\n* Say 3 times calmly: **«سُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الْعَظِيمِ»** (*\"Subhana Rabbiyal 'Adheem\"* — Glory be to my Lord, the Supreme).\n\n### Step 4: Rising from Bowing (*Al-I'tidal*)\n* Rise back to a standing straight posture while saying:\n  * **«سَمِعَ اللَّهُ لِمَنْ حَمِدَهُ»** (*\"Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah\"* — Allah hears whoever praises Him).\n* Once standing completely upright and still, say:\n  * **«رَبَّنَا وَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ»** (*\"Rabbana wa lakal-hamd\"* — Our Lord, and to You belongs all praise).\n\n### Step 5: First Prostration (*As-Sujood*)\n* Say *«اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ»* and descend into prostration.\n* Place 7 contact points firmly on the floor: (1) Forehead and nose, (2 & 3) Both palms flat next to ears/shoulders with fingers together pointing to Qiblah, (4 & 5) Both knees, (6 & 7) Toes of both feet tucked and pointing towards Qiblah.\n* Keep arms elevated off the ground (do not lay forearms flat like a dog).\n* Say 3 times: **«سُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الأَعْلَى»** (*\"Subhana Rabbiyal A'la\"* — Glory be to my Lord, the Most High).\n\n### Step 6: Sitting Between Prostrations (*Al-Jalsah*)\n* Say *«اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ»* and rise to a calm seated position (*Iftirash*—sitting upon the left foot with the right foot upright).\n* Place hands on your thighs and say:\n  * **«رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي، رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي»** (*\"Rabbighfir lee, Rabbighfir lee\"* — My Lord, forgive me; My Lord, forgive me).\n\n### Step 7: Second Prostration\n* Say *«اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ»* and prostrate a second time identically to the first, repeating *«سُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الأَعْلَى»* 3 times.\n* Say *«اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ»* and stand up completely. **You have now completed 1 full Rak'ah!**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Completing the Full Prayers\n\n### For a 2-Rak'ah Prayer (Fajr):\n* Perform Rak'ah 2 identically to Rak'ah 1.\n* After the second Sujood of Rak'ah 2, remain seated on the floor and recite the **Full Tashahhud and Salawat Ibrahimiyyah**.\n* Conclude by turning your head to the right: **«السَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللَّهِ»**, then to the left: **«السَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللَّهِ»**.\n\n### For a 3-Rak'ah Prayer (Maghrib):\n* After Rak'ah 2, sit and recite the First Tashahhud (up to *«wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluh»*).\n* Stand up for Rak'ah 3 (reciting only Al-Fatihah silently).\n* After Rak'ah 3 Sujood, sit for the Full Tashahhud, Salawat Ibrahimiyyah, and Tasleem.\n\n### For a 4-Rak'ah Prayer (Dhuhr, Asr, Isha):\n* Perform Rak'ahs 1 & 2. Sit for First Tashahhud.\n* Stand for Rak'ahs 3 & 4 (reciting only Al-Fatihah silently in each).\n* Sit after Rak'ah 4 for Full Tashahhud, Salawat Ibrahimiyyah, and Tasleem.\n      ",
