        "content": "\n# Module 6: Common Mistakes, Sujood as-Sahw & Special Prayers\n\nIn this module, we address practical scenarios: what to do when you make a mistake, and how to participate in congregational and special prayers.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Common Mistakes in Prayer and How to Avoid Them\n\n* **Rushing Without Stillness (*'Adam at-Tuma'neenah*)**: Moving like a pecking bird between postures. Solution: Pause for at least 3 seconds in each posture.\n* **Looking Around or Gazing at the Sky**: The Prophet ﷺ strictly warned against looking up towards the heavens in prayer (Sahih Muslim 428). Solution: Keep gaze fixed on the prostration spot.\n* **Resting Forearms on the Floor in Sujood**: The Prophet ﷺ prohibited laying forearms flat like a dog (Sahih al-Bukhari 822). Solution: Elevate elbows and keep forearms off the ground.\n* **Preceding the Imam in Congregational Prayer**: Moving to Ruku' or Sujood before the Imam. The Sunnah is to move immediately *after* the Imam finishes saying *Allahu Akbar*.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Prostration of Forgetfulness (*Sujood as-Sahw*)\n\nHuman forgetfulness is natural. Islam provides a clean, standardized remedy called **Sujood as-Sahw** (two prostrations performed at the end of prayer) for three specific reasons:\n\n1. **Addition (*Az-Ziyadah*)**: Accidentally adding an extra Rak'ah, Ruku', or Sujood. Perform 2 prostrations after the Tasleem.\n2. **Omission (*An-Naqs*)**: Accidentally omitting an obligatory act (such as forgetting the middle Tashahhud and standing up). Perform 2 prostrations before the Tasleem.\n3. **Doubt (*Ash-Shakk*)**: Doubting whether you prayed 3 or 4 Rak'ahs. Build upon what you are certain of (the lower number: 3), complete the 4th Rak'ah, and perform 2 prostrations before the Tasleem.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Special & Congregational Prayers\n\n### Friday Prayer (*Salat al-Jumu'ah*)\n* Obligatory upon adult Muslim men in place of Dhuhr prayer.\n* Consists of listening to the **Khutbah** (sermon) followed by **2 Rak'ahs recited aloud** behind the Imam.\n\n### Funeral Prayer (*Salat al-Janazah*)\n* A communal obligation (*Fard Kifayah*) with **no Ruku' or Sujood**, performed standing throughout:\n  * 1st Takbir: Recite Surah Al-Fatihah silently.\n  * 2nd Takbir: Recite Salawat Ibrahimiyyah.\n  * 3rd Takbir: Make sincere Du'a for the deceased.\n  * 4th Takbir: Pause briefly and conclude with Tasleem to the right.\n\n### The Traveler's Prayer (*Salat al-Musafir*)\n* A divine concession (*Rukhsah*): When traveling a qualifying journey (approx. 80km+), the 4-Rak'ah prayers (Dhuhr, Asr, Isha) are shortened (**Qasr**) to 2 Rak'ahs each, and may be combined (**Jam'**) Dhuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha.\n      ",
