        "content": "\n# Module 2: Core Virtues: Truthfulness, Trustworthiness & Humility\n\nNoble character is built upon four foundational pillars that define how a believer speaks, interacts, and carries oneself.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Sidq (Absolute Truthfulness)\n\nTruthfulness is the foundation of all integrity. In Islam, truthfulness applies to three dimensions:\n1. **Truthfulness of Speech (*Sidq al-Lisan*)**: Stating facts accurately, avoiding exaggeration, and never uttering lies—even in jest or sales.\n2. **Truthfulness of Action (*Sidq al-'Amal*)**: Ensuring that one's private actions match one's public words.\n3. **Truthfulness of Intention (*Sidq an-Niyyah*)**: Sincerity in seeking Allah's pleasure.\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ said:\n> **«عَلَيْكُمْ بِالصِّدْقِ، فَإِنَّ الصِّدْقَ يَهْدِي إِلَى الْبِرِّ، وَإِنَّ الْبِرَّ يَهْدِي إِلَى الْجَنَّةِ... وَإِيَّاكُمْ وَالْكَذِبَ، فَإِنَّ الْكَذِبَ يَهْدِي إِلَى الْفُجُورِ، وَإِنَّ الْفُجُورَ يَهْدِي إِلَى النَّارِ»**  \n> *\"Adhere strictly to truthfulness, for truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise... And beware of lying, for lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to Hellfire.\"* (Sahih al-Bukhari 6094, Sahih Muslim 2607).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Amanah (Trustworthiness & Integrity)\n\n*Amanah* encompasses every responsibility entrusted to you:\n* **Fulfilling Promises & Contracts**: Keeping your word in business, employment, and agreements.\n* **Guarding Secrets**: Keeping private confidences shared by friends, spouses, or colleagues.\n* **Professional Diligence**: Performing work with excellence (*Itqan*) and not stealing time or resources from employers.\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ warned: *«لاَ إِيمَانَ لِمَنْ لاَ أَمَانَةَ لَهُ، وَلاَ دِينَ لِمَنْ لاَ عَهْدَ لَهُ»* (*\"There is no faith for the one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for the one who does not keep promises\"* — Musnad Ahmad 12383).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Haya' (Dignified Modesty & Moral Sensitivity)\n\n*Haya'* is an innate spiritual sensitivity that causes a person to shrink away from vulgarity, indecency, and sin out of reverence for Allah.\n* The Prophet ﷺ declared: *«الْحَيَاءُ شُعْبَةٌ مِنَ الإِيمَانِ»* (*\"Haya' is a major branch of faith\"* — Sahih al-Bukhari 9).\n* *«الْحَيَاءُ لاَ يَأْتِي إِلاَّ بِخَيْرٍ»* (*\"Haya' brings nothing but pure goodness\"* — Sahih al-Bukhari 6117).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tawadu' (Humility) vs. Kibr (Arrogance)\n\n* **Tawadu' (Humility)**: Treating every human with dignity, accepting truth regardless of who speaks it, and recognizing that all your talents are gifts from Allah.\n* **Kibr (Arrogance)**: The spiritual poison that caused Iblees (Satan) to be expelled from divine mercy.\n* The Prophet ﷺ gave the definitive definition of arrogance:\n  > **«الْكِبْرُ بَطَرُ الْحَقِّ وَغَمْطُ النَّاسِ»**  \n  > *\"Arrogance is rejecting the truth and looking down upon people with contempt.\"* (Sahih Muslim 91).\n      ",
