        "content": "\n# Module 4: Social Etiquette (Adab al-Mu'asharah) & Guarding the Tongue\n\nIslam provides complete, sophisticated social etiquette (*Adab al-Mu'asharah*) that fosters mutual love, dignity, and harmony in society.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Spreading the Greeting of Peace (*Ifsha' as-Salam*)\n\nThe universal Islamic greeting is **«السَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللَّهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ»** (*\"Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings\"*).\n* The Prophet ﷺ said:\n  > *«لاَ تَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ حَتَّى تُؤْمِنُوا، وَلاَ تُؤْمِنُوا حَتَّى تَحَابُّوا، أَوَلاَ أَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَى شَيْءٍ إِذَا فَعَلْتُمُوهُ تَحَابَبْتُمْ؟ أَفْشُوا السَّلاَمَ بَيْنَكُمْ»*  \n  > *\"You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not guide you to something which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread the Salam among you.\"* (Sahih Muslim 54).\n\n### Etiquette of Salam:\n* The rider greets the walker; the walker greets the sitting; the smaller group greets the larger group; and the younger greets the elder (Sahih al-Bukhari 6231).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Prophetic Manners of Eating and Drinking\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ taught young 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah (RA) the core rules of eating:\n> **«يَا غُلاَمُ: سَمِّ اللَّهَ، وَكُلْ بِيَمِينِكَ، وَكُلْ مِمَّا يَلِيكَ»**  \n> *\"O young boy: Mention the Name of Allah (say Bismillah), eat with your right hand, and eat from that which is nearest to you.\"* (Sahih al-Bukhari 5376, Sahih Muslim 2022).\n\n### Additional Dining Etiquette:\n* **Say Bismillah** before beginning; if forgotten, say: *«بِسْمِ اللَّهِ أَوَّلَهُ وَآخِرَهُ»* (*Bismillahi awwalahu wa akhirahu*).\n* **Eat and drink with the right hand**: The Prophet ﷺ forbade eating or drinking with the left hand, as Satan eats with his left hand (Sahih Muslim 2020).\n* **Drink while sitting in 2 or 3 calm sips**, avoiding blowing into the drink.\n* **Praise Allah upon finishing**: Say *«الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ»*.\n* **Never criticize food**: If the Prophet ﷺ liked food, he ate it; if he disliked it, he simply left it without disparaging the cook (Sahih al-Bukhari 5409).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Guarding the Tongue (*Hifdh al-Lisan*)\n\nThe tongue is small in size but colossal in consequence. Sins of the tongue destroy righteous deeds:\n\n### 1. Gheebah (Backbiting)\n* The Prophet ﷺ defined backbiting: *“Mentioning your brother with something he dislikes (in his absence).”* Someone asked: *“What if what I say is true about him?”* He replied: *“If it is true, you have backbitten him; and if it is not true, you have slandered him (Buhtan).”* (Sahih Muslim 2589).\n* The Qur'an likens backbiting to **eating the dead flesh of your own brother** (Surah Al-Hujurat 49:12).\n\n### 2. Nameemah (Malicious Tale-Bearing / Gossip)\n* Carrying speech between people with the intent to cause discord and break relationships.\n* The Prophet ﷺ warned: *«لاَ يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ قَتَّاتٌ [نَمَّامٌ]»* (*\"The tale-bearer will not enter Paradise\"* — Sahih al-Bukhari 6056, Sahih Muslim 105).\n      ",
