        "id": "manners-5",
        "number": 5,
        "title": "Module 5: Verified Daily Supplications (Duas for Everyday Life)",
        "subtitle": "Waking up, sleeping, entering/leaving home, bathroom, eating, and travel with Arabic, transliteration & references",
        "readingTime": "22 min",
        "summary": "Learn and memorize essential daily prophetic supplications (Duas) for waking, sleeping, leaving home, bathroom, eating, and traveling, sourced from Hisn al-Muslim.",
        "objectives": [
          "Memorize essential daily supplications with correct Arabic pronunciation and meanings",
          "Understand the spiritual protection and barakah unlocked by daily prophetic Duas",
          "Master the supplications for waking up, entering/leaving home, bathroom, and travel",
          "Integrate daily Duas smoothly into your everyday routine"
        ],
        "content": "\n# Module 5: Verified Daily Supplications (Duas for Everyday Life)\n\nDu'a is described by the Prophet ﷺ as **the essence of worship** (*«الدُّعَاءُ هُوَ الْعِبَادَةُ»* — Tirmidhi 2969). By learning the Prophet's daily supplications, your entire day from waking to sleeping becomes illuminated with divine connection.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Waking Up & Going to Sleep\n\n### Upon Waking Up:\n> **«الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي أَحْيَانَا بَعْدَ مَا أَمَاتَنَا وَإِلَيْهِ النُّشُورُ»**  \n> *Alhamdu lillahilladhi ahyana ba'da ma amatana wa ilayhin-nushoor.*  \n> *\"All praise is due to Allah, who gave us life after having caused us to die, and unto Him is the final resurrection.\"*  \n> 📜 **Source**: Sahih al-Bukhari (6312), Sahih Muslim (2711).\n\n### Before Sleeping:\n> **«بِاسْمِكَ رَبِّي وَضَعْتُ جَنْبِي وَبِكَ أَرْفَعُهُ، فَإِنْ أَمْسَكْتَ نَفْسِي فَارْحَمْهَا، وَإِنْ أَرْسَلْتَهَا فَاحْفَظْهَا بِمَا تَحْفَظُ بِهِ عِبَادَكَ الصَّالِحِينَ»**  \n> *Bismika Rabbi wada'tu janbi wa bika arfa'uh, fa-in amsakta nafsi farhamha, wa-in arsaltaha fahfadh-ha bima tahfadhu bihi 'ibadakas-salihin.*  \n> *\"In Your Name, my Lord, I lay down my side and with Your Name I raise it. If You take my soul, have mercy upon it, and if You return it, protect it with that which You protect Your righteous servants.\"*  \n> 📜 **Source**: Sahih al-Bukhari (6320), Sahih Muslim (2714).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Leaving & Entering the Home\n\n### When Leaving the House (Divine Protection & Guidance):\n> **«بِسْمِ اللَّهِ، تَوَكَّلْتُ عَلَى اللَّهِ، وَلاَ حَوْلَ وَلاَ قُوَّةَ إِلاَّ بِاللَّهِ»**  \n> *Bismillahi, tawakkaltu 'alallahi, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah.*  \n> *\"In the Name of Allah, I place my trust in Allah; there is no power nor might except with Allah.\"*  \n> *(When said, angels proclaim: 'You are guided, defended, and protected, and Satan retreats from you!')*  \n> 📜 **Source**: Sunan Abi Dawud (5095), Jami' at-Tirmidhi (3426) — Sahih.\n\n### When Entering the House:\n> **«بِسْمِ اللَّهِ وَلَجْنَا، وَبِسْمِ اللَّهِ خَرَجْنَا، وَعَلَى رَبِّنَا تَوَكَّلْنَا»**  \n> *Bismillahi walajna, wa bismillahi kharajna, wa 'ala Rabbina tawakkalna.*  \n> *\"In the Name of Allah we enter, and in the Name of Allah we leave, and upon our Lord we place our trust.\"* (Followed by saying Salam to the family).  \n> 📜 **Source**: Sunan Abi Dawud (5096), Sahih Muslim (2018).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Entering & Leaving the Bathroom\n\n* **Entering (Seeking refuge from impurity & harm)**:\n  > *«بِسْمِ اللَّهِ، اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنَ الْخُبُثِ وَالْخَبَائِثِ»*  \n  > *Bismillahi, Allahumma inni a'udhu bika minal-khubuthi wal-khaba'ith.*  \n  > *\"In the Name of Allah. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female foul spirits.\"*  \n  > 📜 **Source**: Sahih al-Bukhari (142), Sahih Muslim (375).\n* **Exiting**:\n  > *«غُفْرَانَكَ»* (*Ghufranak* — *\"I ask Your forgiveness, O Allah\"*).  \n  > 📜 **Source**: Sunan Abi Dawud (30), Jami' at-Tirmidhi (7) — Sahih.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Before & After Eating\n\n* **Before Eating**: *«بِسْمِ اللَّهِ»* (*Bismillah*).\n* **After Eating**:\n  > **«الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي أَطْعَمَنِي هَذَا وَرَزَقَنِيهِ مِنْ غَيْرِ حَوْلٍ مِنِّي وَلاَ قُوَّةٍ»**  \n  > *Alhamdu lillahilladhi at'amani hadha wa razaqaneehi min ghayri hawlin minnee wa la quwwah.*  \n  > *\"Praise be to Allah Who fed me this and provided it for me without any power or strength from myself.\"*  \n  > *(Forgives all past minor sins!)*  \n  > 📜 **Source**: Jami' at-Tirmidhi (3458), Sunan Abi Dawud (4023) — Hasan-Sahih.\n\n---\n\n## 5. When Traveling (*Du'a as-Safar*)\n\n> **«سُبْحَانَ الَّذِي سَخَّرَ لَنَا هَذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لَهُ مُقْرِنِينَ وَإِنَّا إِلَى رَبِّنَا لَمُنْقَلِبُونَ. اللَّهُمَّ إِنَّا نَسْأَلُكَ فِي سَفَرِنَا هَذَا الْبِرَّ وَالتَّقْوَى، وَمِنَ الْعَمَلِ مَا تَرْضَى...»**  \n> *Subhanalladhi sakh-khara lana hadha wa ma kunna lahu muqrineen, wa inna ila Rabbina lamunqaliboon. Allahumma inna nas'aluka fee safarina hadhal-birra wat-taqwa, wa minal-'amali ma tarda...*  \n> *\"Glory be to Him Who has subjected this to us, and we could never have achieved it by ourselves. And surely, unto our Lord we are returning. O Allah, we ask You in this journey of ours for righteousness, piety, and actions that please You...\"*  \n> 📜 **Source**: Sahih Muslim (1342).\n      ",
