        "content": "# Chapter 4: Sentence Building & French Grammar Foundations\n\nMastering French verb conjugation unlocks your ability to generate unlimited sentences.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Regular Group 1 Verbs (-ER Verbs)\n\nGroup 1 (-ER verbs) constitutes over 80% of all French verbs. To conjugate, drop the **-er** and add the personal endings:\n\n```\nParler (To speak) ➔ Stem: Parl-\n• Je parl-e       (I speak)        ➔ /paʁl/\n• Tu parl-es      (You speak)      ➔ /paʁl/\n• Il/Elle parl-e  (He/She speaks)  ➔ /paʁl/\n• Nous parl-ons   (We speak)       ➔ /paʁ.lɔ̃/\n• Vous parl-ez    (You speak)      ➔ /paʁ.le/\n• Ils/Elles parl-ent (They speak)  ➔ /paʁl/\n```\n\n> **Pronunciation Secret:** 4 of the 6 forms (*je parle, tu parles, il parle, ils parlent*) sound 100% identical!\n\n---\n\n## 2. French Negation (Ne ... Pas)\n\nTo make a sentence negative, place **ne** (or **n'** before a vowel) before the verb and **pas** after it:\n- *Je comprends.* ➔ *Je **ne** comprends **pas**.* (I do not understand).\n- *Il habite ici.* ➔ *Il **n'**habite **pas** ici.* (He does not live here).",
