        "transcript": "Asking questions in Japanese is remarkably straightforward: simply attach the question particle か (ka) to the end of any declarative sentence, without changing the word order. To ask for specific information, use interrogative pronouns: 何 (nani/nan) for 'what', どこ (doko) for 'where', いつ (itsu) for 'when', だれ / どなた (dare / donata) for 'who', どうして / なぜ (doushite / naze) for 'why', and いくら (ikura) for 'how much'. When answering in the affirmative, say 'Hai' followed by the verb; in the negative, say 'Iie' followed by the negative verb ending '-masen'.",
