        "transcript": "Somali culture is deeply hospitable, and social interaction begins with respectful greetings. The most common informal greeting is 'Iska warran?' (How are you? / What's your news?), to which you reply 'Waan fiicanahay' (I am fine) or 'Nabad' (Peace). Another classic greeting is 'Nabad miyaa?' (Is there peace?), replied with 'Waa nabad' (It is peaceful). Time-based greetings include 'Subax wanaagsan' (Good morning), 'Galab wanaagsan' (Good afternoon), and 'Habeen wanaagsan' (Good night). Politeness markers include 'Fadlan' (Please), 'Mahadsanid' (Thank you), and 'Adaa mudan' (You are welcome). To say goodbye, use 'Nabad gelyo' (Go in peace).",
