        "content": "# Chapter 3: Greetings & Polite Expressions\n\nGreetings (*Salaanta*) are essential in Somali daily culture and demonstrate warmth and respect.\n\n---\n\n## Everyday Greetings & Responses\n\n| Greeting | Meaning | Response | Response Meaning |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Iska warran?** | How are you? | **Waan fiicanahay** | I am fine |\n| **Nabad miyaa?** | Is there peace? | **Waa nabad** | It is peaceful |\n| **Sidee tahay?** | How are you doing? | **Waan ladnahay** | I am doing well |\n| **Maxaa cusub?** | What is new? | **Waxba / Khayr** | Nothing / All good |\n\n---\n\n## Time-Based Greetings\n\n- **Subax wanaagsan** — Good morning\n- **Galab wanaagsan** — Good afternoon\n- **Habeen wanaagsan** — Good evening / Good night\n- **Habeen wanaagsan, hurdada ku raaxayso** — Good night, enjoy your sleep\n\n---\n\n## Polite Courtesies\n\n- **Fadlan** — Please\n- **Mahadsanid** — Thank you (Aad baad u mahadsan tahay = Thank you very much)\n- **Adaa mudan** — You are welcome\n- **I saamax / Raali noqo** — Excuse me / Forgive me\n- **Nabad gelyo** — Goodbye (Go in peace)",
