        "transcript": "Somali verbs carry rich information. Basic root verbs include: Tag (go), Imoow (come), Cun (eat), Cab (drink), Qor (write), Akhri (read), Joog (stay/stop), Arag (see), and Hadal (speak). Subject pronouns are: Aniga (I / me), Adiga (You), Isaga (He / him), Iyada (She / her), Innaga / Anaga (We / us), Idinka (You plural), and Iyaga (They / them). In standard sentences, focus markers and verbal pronouns such as 'waan' (I + statement marker), 'waxaad' (you), 'wuxuu' (he), 'waxay' (she), 'waxaan' (we/I) connect the subject to the verb. Present progressive is formed with '-ayaa' (e.g. Waan tagayaa = I am going). Past tense uses '-ay' or '-tay' (e.g. Waan tagay = I went).",
