        "content": "# Chapter 7: Common Verbs & Sentence Building\n\nVerbs (*Falka*) bring Somali sentences to life.\n\n---\n\n## Essential Root Verbs\n\n| Verb (Root) | Meaning | Present Continuous (I am...) | Past (I ...ed) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Tag** | Go | **Waan tagayaa** (I am going) | **Waan tagay** (I went) |\n| **Imoow** | Come | **Waan imanayaa** (I am coming) | **Waan imid** (I came) |\n| **Cun** | Eat | **Waan cunayaa** (I am eating) | **Waan cunay** (I ate) |\n| **Cab** | Drink | **Waan cabayaa** (I am drinking) | **Waan cabay** (I drank) |\n| **Qor** | Write | **Waan qorayaa** (I am writing) | **Waan qoray** (I wrote) |\n| **Akhri** | Read | **Waan akhrinayaa** (I am reading) | **Waan akhriyey** (I read) |\n| **Hadal** | Speak | **Waan hadlayaa** (I am speaking) | **Waan hadlay** (I spoke) |\n\n---\n\n## Pronouns & Statement Markers\n\n- **Aniga** (I) $\\rightarrow$ **Waan...** (I...)\n- **Adiga** (You) $\\rightarrow$ **Waxaad...** (You...)\n- **Isaga** (He) $\\rightarrow$ **Wuxuu...** (He...)\n- **Iyada** (She) $\\rightarrow$ **Waxay...** (She...)\n- **Annaga** (We) $\\rightarrow$ **Waxaan...** (We...)\n- **Iyaga** (They) $\\rightarrow$ **Waxay...** (They...)",
