        "content": "# Chapter 10: Reading Practice & Course Review\n\nCelebrate your journey into Af-Soomaali with authentic cultural readings and wisdom.\n\n---\n\n## Reading Passage: Subax Cusub (A New Morning)\n\n> *Subax kasta, qorraxdu waxay ka soo baxdaa bariga. Cali wuxuu kacaa goor hore. Wuxuu cabbaa koob shaah ah oo caano leh, wuxuuna cunaa canjeero kulul. Cali wuxuu jecel yahay inuu barto luqadaha cusub. Wuxuu aadaa dugsiga si uu wax u barto, maxaa yeelay 'Aqoon la'aan waa iftiin la'aan'. Barashada Af-Soomaaligu waxay furtay albaabbo badan oo saaxiibtinnimo iyo aqoon ah.*\n\n### English Translation:\n*Every morning, the sun rises from the east. Ali wakes up early. He drinks a cup of tea with milk and eats hot canjeero. Ali loves learning new languages. He goes to school to study, because 'Without knowledge, there is no light'. Learning Somali has opened many doors of friendship and knowledge.*\n\n---\n\n## Classic Somali Proverbs (Maahmaahyo)\n\n1. **Aqoon la'aan waa iftiin la'aan**  \n   *Meaning:* Ignorance is darkness; knowledge is light.\n\n2. **Far keligeed fool ma dhaqdo**  \n   *Meaning:* A single finger cannot wash a face (Together we achieve more).\n\n3. **Gacmo wadajir bay wax ku gooyaan**  \n   *Meaning:* Hands working together cut through anything (Unity creates power).\n\n---\n\n## Hambalyo! (Hearty Congratulations!)\nYou have successfully completed the 10 chapters of **Somali Language Learning** on FAHMRISE!\nContinue speaking Af-Soomaali, connecting with communities, and exploring the richness of East African culture.",
